WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:02.679
An archaeologist enters the temple chamber.

00:00:02.679 --> 00:00:08.200
It’s clear that whatever is inside, the
people who kept it did not want it found,

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.250
but there are no chests full of gold and jewels
or ancient artifacts piled in the corners.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:19.539
In fact, the room is completely empty except
for one small statue on a pedestal.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:24.640
Upon closer investigation, it is made of green
soapstone and appears to be carved into the

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.239
shape of a seated skeletal figure.

00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:32.230
It seems harmless, and the archaeologist stares
at it - until he hears one of his colleagues

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.829
talking outside.

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:37.160
He turns back to answer them before looking
back at the statue.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.940
Which is no longer on its pedestal.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.730
The archaeologist panics, and calls for someone
else to come check this out.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:48.780
But he only manages to get a few words out
about the statue’s mysterious absence, before

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.870
he starts feeling an odd tightness in his
chest.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:55.789
He tries to head for the door, but everything
starts going dark.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:59.719
He collapses to the floor, dying instantly.

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:05.360
And just as quickly, the mysterious green
statue reappears - this time located directly

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.830
on the chest of the deceased scientist, awaiting
its next viewer.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.830
SCP-689, also known as the Haunter in the
Dark, was first discovered in the early 20th

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:21.250
century, as German explorers searched Indian
architectural sites for valuable artifacts.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:26.890
The green soapstone statue, only thirty centimeters
in height, isn’t particularly light, but

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:32.070
it’s also not large or heavy enough to cause
any problems for those looking to take it.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.630
Those who have studied it believe the skeletal
figure, which is seated with its hands clasped

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.680
over its knees, represents an ancient deity
of the underworld.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:45.410
After its discovery, the statue’s location
was briefly unknown, but it was later obtained

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:50.220
by the United States’ Office of Strategic
Services from German hands after the end of

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.610
the Second World War.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:56.760
And that’s when its dangerous properties
became clear for the first time.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:02.250
While SCP-689 appears to be a standard inert
statue, this only holds true if it is being

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.700
watched by at least one person.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.311
When it becomes dangerous is if it is in the
presence of a person who watches it, then

00:02:09.311 --> 00:02:11.490
takes their eyes off the statue.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:16.140
Thankfully, SCP-689’s anomalous effects
aren’t triggered by normal behavior like

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.530
blinking, but as soon as eye contact is fully
broken, like when someone looks away from

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:24.470
it completely, the statue will vanish.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:30.580
It will then re-appear fifteen to twenty seconds
later - and bring with it a deadly curse.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:36.230
Because each time SCP-689 vanishes, it takes
a life.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:41.870
In under twenty seconds, one person who has
previously seen SCP-689 and broke eye contact

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.220
with it will die spontaneously.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.560
The cause of death is always some sort of
natural cause, but it ranges from mundane

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:53.861
causes like heart attacks and strokes to sudden
ruptures of internal organs - including, in

00:02:53.861 --> 00:02:58.730
some cases, every major organ in the body
rupturing at once.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:04.390
If only one person has currently viewed SCP-689
and is alive, the statue will cause their

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.480
death and immediately appear atop their body.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:13.230
But when there is more than one possible target,
the statue becomes far more dangerous.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:17.850
This effect only works on humans, but anyone
who has ever viewed the statue is vulnerable.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:23.130
It’s as if it keeps a list of everyone who
has ever seen it and broken eye contact, and

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:27.020
when it has the chance, it starts picking
people off that list.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.840
And it doesn’t matter where in the world
they are located.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.690
The statue has been shown to be able to teleport
long distances and appear on the body of someone

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:37.000
who might have viewed it years ago.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.250
There seems to be no way to predict in what
order the statue will claim its victim.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:46.660
However, a disturbing pattern of who the Haunter
in the Dark decides is next has emerged.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:51.721
When the statue has choices available to it,
it seems to often target a victim who is in

00:03:51.721 --> 00:03:53.310
a large crowd.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:58.380
That means that in an instant, hundreds of
people could see the statue and become future

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.380
targets.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:04.450
As every time an eye is taken off the statue,
it could teleport and claim another life,

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:09.220
this raises the possibility of a horrific
chain effect scenario, where the statue could

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.760
teleport endlessly and rack up a massive body
count in mere minutes.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.820
Which is why the Foundation has become determined
that it never be seen again.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:23.629
The cell holding SCP-689 is one of the most
secure in the entire SCP Foundation, because

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:27.889
unlike other Keter class objects, it gives
very little warning.

00:04:27.889 --> 00:04:33.000
If it is seen, it can be gone in a second
with no way of knowing where it is.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.319
And depending on how many possible targets
are out there, it could be anywhere in the

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:38.449
world.

00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:42.990
That is why it is currently encased in a large
concrete chamber, surrounded by high-intensity

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.080
sodium iodide lights.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:49.620
Each of these lights has a separate power
supply, so there is no chance of a total power

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:50.620
failure.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:55.360
And for those tasked with keeping it safe,
it’s one of the hardest jobs in the Foundation.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.259
Three people are on duty at SCP-689’s cell
at all times.

00:04:59.259 --> 00:05:04.339
Two D-Class personnel are stationed inside
the chamber, and a Level 2 agent is stationed

00:05:04.339 --> 00:05:05.889
in the control chamber.

00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:10.650
The D-Class agents have one job - to never
take their eyes off the statue.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:14.979
They can alternate breaks, but the statue
must never be allowed to be unobserved for

00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:16.500
even a second.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.180
And because each person who has seen the statue
is a security risk, the D-class agents are

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:26.159
equipped with instant-kill devices so they
can be terminated from afar rather than being

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.830
potential targets.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:31.360
The Level 2 Agent, meanwhile, has a very different
job.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.479
This is one of the most specialized tasks
in the entire Foundation, because the agent

00:05:35.479 --> 00:05:40.480
must be either blind or equipped with a helmet
that completely blocks their vision, which

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:44.479
they must wear for their entire SCP-689 shift.

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:48.680
All control features in the chamber are designed
to be operated by someone without the ability

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:53.800
to see, and the operator is not to remove
their helmet under any circumstances - or

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:59.009
they risk termination themselves as a potential
security risk and escape vector.

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:04.039
But don’t worry, even if the statue still
manages to escape its chamber, the Foundation

00:06:04.039 --> 00:06:05.080
has a plan.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:08.639
Just don’t tell staff assigned to 689 what
it is.

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:12.559
In the event of a containment breach or failure
of the lights in the statue’s chamber, the

00:06:12.559 --> 00:06:17.220
first priority is to terminate any D-Class
or Level 1 observers who may have been exposed

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.009
to the Haunter in the Dark.

00:06:19.009 --> 00:06:23.319
This is to reduce potential targets, and while
higher-level staff will be retained in most

00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:26.969
cases, this only goes for the first containment
failure.

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:31.860
The Foundation will then deploy a retrieval
team of blind agents or those wearing vision-blocking

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.150
headsets.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:37.139
Equipped with echolocation tech, they’ll
partner with D-Class observers to track down

00:06:37.139 --> 00:06:39.740
everyone who is known to have viewed the statue.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:44.340
The statue will invariably appear and lead
to the death of one of these people, so knowledge

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.860
of these potential targets is key to containment.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.539
Then comes the challenge of returning it to
containment.

00:06:50.539 --> 00:06:55.259
As soon as the statue is located, a perimeter
is established with coverings put up to avoid

00:06:55.259 --> 00:06:57.789
any outside viewers catching a glimpse of
it.

00:06:57.789 --> 00:07:02.569
The D-class observers enter the perimeter
and are transported back to the facility together

00:07:02.569 --> 00:07:07.240
to ensure it never falls out of sight until
it is safely back in its chamber and its containment

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.729
protocols are put back in place.

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:12.839
But what is actually known about this deadly
statue?

00:07:12.839 --> 00:07:17.479
Because of how dangerous and fast-moving the
statue is, any attempts to study its properties

00:07:17.479 --> 00:07:22.020
must be approved by the presiding scientist
and are carefully scrutinized.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:26.680
The curiosity to figure out its mysteries
is always tempered by the fact that any scientist

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:31.900
interested may be subject to summary termination
should it breach containment again.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:36.889
Its origins are unknown and but it is thought
to be at least several centuries old, and

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:40.399
its form is believed to be based on a God
of the underworld.

00:07:40.399 --> 00:07:45.319
This would explain its one function - ensuring
people make a swift visit to the afterlife.

00:07:45.319 --> 00:07:51.150
It does not seem to have any direct hostility
towards humans or SCP personnel and has not

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:56.400
given any indication that it is sapient or
intelligent, but it does seem to want to spread

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:01.099
as quickly as possible - and it may be able
to sense where its best targets with the greatest

00:08:01.099 --> 00:08:03.379
potential to spread are located.

00:08:03.379 --> 00:08:08.969
This has led many to compare it to one of
the SCP Foundation’s most notorious residents.

00:08:08.969 --> 00:08:14.520
SCP-173 is another statue that poses a grave
danger to anyone who looks at it the right

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.520
way.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:20.729
Similar to SCP-689, it is frozen in place
and requires anyone who enters its containment

00:08:20.729 --> 00:08:22.979
unit to look directly at it.

00:08:22.979 --> 00:08:27.860
Any breaking of eye contact can be deadly,
and its more strict in its definition of breaking

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.800
eye contact than 689 is.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:35.089
Simply taking your eyes off it for even a
second, even to blink is enough to seal your

00:08:35.089 --> 00:08:36.089
fate.

00:08:36.089 --> 00:08:40.539
But SCP-173 doesn’t use supernatural powers
to claim its victim.

00:08:40.539 --> 00:08:45.540
This large concrete statue instead becomes
mobile and extremely violent when eye contact

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.910
is broken, killing its targets by strangulation
or breaking the neck.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:54.260
While this entity has killed many personnel
since its containment, it doesn’t seem to

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:59.911
have the same ability of SCP-689 to teleport
to a completely different location, which

00:08:59.911 --> 00:09:03.720
means it is actually less of a threat than
the Haunter in the Dark.

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:08.529
But the two statues’ similar MO of killing
when eye contact is broken has led some to

00:09:08.529 --> 00:09:13.370
speculate a connection - despite one being
of modern construction and the other being

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.510
old, possibly even ancient.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:20.139
But only one of these statues poses a potential
end-of-the-world scenario.

00:09:20.139 --> 00:09:25.510
Which is why the Foundation is so concerned
about SCP-689 breaching containment.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:31.600
SCP-689 might just be among the hardest anomalies
to get back in the bottle once it escapes.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.259
If it appears far outside containment, in
a crowded scene, it now has hundreds of new

00:09:36.259 --> 00:09:37.890
potential targets.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:42.490
By the time the Foundation tracks it down
to its past location, it will have likely

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:47.339
teleported again - and there seems to be no
limit to how many lives it can claim in a

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:48.550
set time.

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:53.259
That means that as it racks up more targets
and teleports into crowds, it could escalate

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:57.000
into a major threat to Earth’s entire population.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:02.399
With SCP-689 seeming to be able to kill anything
that breaks eye contact with it, there are

00:10:02.399 --> 00:10:06.899
some in the Foundation who wonder if it should
be used against the most notorious captive

00:10:06.899 --> 00:10:12.060
of the SCP Foundation - SCP-682.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:16.690
This rage-filled, indestructible, regenerating
beast has been a thorn in the Foundation’s

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.319
side for years.

00:10:18.319 --> 00:10:22.850
It has cost countless lives of agents and
personnel with its many containment breaches

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:28.300
and so far the Foundation has been unable
to terminate it by any conventional means.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:33.779
But SCP-689 isn’t exactly what you would
call “conventional means.”

00:10:33.779 --> 00:10:38.940
It simply triggers an invariably fatal reaction
within the body of whoever it targets - which

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:44.930
means it could possibly be the only thing
that could kill SCP-682 permanently.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:49.129
The risks of pitting these two anomalies against
each other are immense though.

00:10:49.129 --> 00:10:54.860
Not only does any interaction with SCP-682
carry risks of yet another catastrophic containment

00:10:54.860 --> 00:11:01.519
breach, but moving the volatile SCP-689 puts
everyone, not just those in the Foundation,

00:11:01.519 --> 00:11:02.800
at risk too.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:07.710
The proposed plan involves exposing the two,
then immediately turning off the lights.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:13.300
But for this experiment to be pulled off safely,
every personnel who has seen SCP-689 must

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:17.990
either be terminated or placed in the same
containment chamber - giving the statue no

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:21.329
choice but to eventually choose SCP-682.

00:11:21.329 --> 00:11:26.899
To improve the chance of success, the doctors
planning this operation have suggested terminating

00:11:26.899 --> 00:11:31.060
all D-class personnel in advance to better
the odds.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:36.360
Should this experiment ever be approved though,
a failure could be truly catastrophic.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:41.670
SCP-682 has already shown itself able to come
back from things that are seemingly impossible

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:47.040
to survive, including having the majority
of its body destroyed with only atoms remaining,

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.430
and yet it was still able to regenerate back.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.459
Who’s to say it couldn’t survive a heart
attack or organ rupture too?

00:11:53.459 --> 00:11:57.730
There is also the risk of 682 gaining the
power used against it.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:04.240
The only thing worse than SCP-682, is an SCP-682
that can now teleport around the world to

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.980
kill anyone who has ever looked at it.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:11.560
But even with these risks, the experiment
has not been officially ruled out.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:16.009
Could one of the Foundation’s deadliest
Keter class anomalies be the solution to another?

00:12:16.009 --> 00:12:21.370
It’s under advisement, but for right now,
the Foundation is keeping a very close eye

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:26.379
on SCP-689 - in more ways than one.

00:12:26.379 --> 00:12:31.680
For more on the Foundation’s first killer
statue, check out “SCP-173 - The Sculpture

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:37.230
Tale”, or watch “Termination Attempts
SCP-682” for just how hard this lizard is

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:37.559
to kill.

